# Bulma UI conventions

- Bulma is pure CSS. Do not add JS UI libraries for what CSS or the browser already does.
- Use native inputs (`date`, `time`, `color`, `range`), `<details>`, and `<dialog>` before reaching for components.
- Layout with `.columns`/`.column` and `.container`; use Bulma helper classes over custom CSS.
- The few JS-needing pieces (navbar burger, modal, dropdown-on-click) get a few inline lines, never a framework.
- Accessibility is required: labels tied to inputs, `aria-label` on icon buttons, `aria-expanded` on toggles, never color-only signals.
- Load Bulma via the project's existing setup; don't introduce a new build pipeline.
- Extract reusable markup into Blade components (anonymous `<x-...>` in `resources/views/components/` first; class component only when logic requires it). Use `@props`/slots and rely on `{{ }}` auto-escaping; never `{!! !!}` user input.
- Interactive/stateful UI is a Livewire component, not a plain Blade one — see `ai/skills/livewire/SKILL.md` and its security policy.

Full guidance: `ai/skills/bulma-ui/SKILL.md`.
